      "reasons": [
        "The definition is too narrow for the term: it describes glabrous skin only as the skin surface of the hand, but the term generally means hairless skin and is not limited to the hand in the packet.",
        "It adds unsupported specificity by framing this as a touch-research context with contact through textures or tools; the packet discusses vibrations in glabrous skin of the hand, but not this as the definition of the term itself.",
        "It loosely recasts the mechanism as spreading vibration signals to tactile receptors; the packet specifically refers to Pacinian corpuscles and PC afferents, so the wording overgeneralizes the source evidence."
